    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Stacked on #510: this PR's base is its branch `510-devonthink-remove-cmd-shift-d`.\n- Merge #510 first, then retarget this PR to `main` (GitHub does it when the base branch is deleted).\n- If merged out of order, nothing breaks, but the Cmd+Shift+D removal comes along with this PR.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `Caps+Option+1` to `Caps+Option+7` pick the colour directly (1 Red, 2 Green, 3 Blue, 4 Yellow, 5 Orange, 6 Purple, 7 Grey) and start highlighting.\n- `Caps+c` cycling stays: it is still handy to step through colours, and it shares the new `setColor` function.\n- `Caps+Option+Shift+1..7` only set the colour and do not start highlighting. This is for recolouring highlights selected in the Annotations inspector.\n- Keys work only while DEVONthink is in front.\n- `aerospace-keys.lua` also opens the Caps layer when Option is already held, so either press order works.\n\n## Clash check\n\n- Caps+1 to 9 are AeroSpace workspaces, so plain numbers could not be used.\n- Caps+Option+anything is unused in the layer, so there is no clash. Option only reaches Hammerspoon, never Emacs, so it does not become Meta.\n- Caps+Ctrl+h/j/k/l (join-with) and Caps+Shift+number (move to workspace) are untouched.\n\n## Recolouring several highlights (unverified)\n\n- I found no DEVONthink scripting call for annotation colours, so there is no direct way to recolour a selection.\n- `Caps+Option+Shift+N` runs the same Format > Highlight Color item. If DEVONthink applies it to the annotations selected in the inspector, it recolours them; if not, it only changes the colour for new highlights.\n- Please test it with several selected annotations and tell me what happens.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [ ] In DEVONthink, Caps+Option+1 through 7: the alert shows Red, Green, Blue, Yellow, Orange, Purple, Grey, and highlight mode starts.\n- [ ] Select text in a PDF and press Caps+Option+4: it highlights in Yellow.\n- [ ] Press Caps+Option first, then Caps (opposite order): the key still works.\n- [ ] Caps+c still cycles through the colours.\n- [ ] Select several highlights in the Annotations inspector, press Caps+Option+Shift+3: note whether they turn Blue.\n- [ ] Caps+3 (no Option) still switches to AeroSpace workspace 3, in DEVONthink and elsewhere.\n- [ ] In other apps, Caps+Option+number does nothing.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
